  - measurement error
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  An empirical audit of a commercial search-augmented answer endpoint (Exa /answer) on
  expertise verification and biographical resolution claims anchored to OpenAlex authorship
  records and SEC Section 16 filings. The endpoint confirms 96.0% of attested expertise
  claims while affirming 16.8% of adjacent-subfield, 13.2% of adjacent-field, and 8.4% of
  different-domain claims with no matching OpenAlex work (n=250 per stratum), with stated
  confidence pinned at ceiling and worse than a constant forecast (Brier 0.1191 vs 0.1005).
  Alongside the empirical results, the paper documents five automated-evaluation failure modes
  caught by row-level inspection. The code and results are MIT, the paper CC BY 4.0.
